  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Learn enrage transition cues: eye glow, aura activation, and roar wind-up differ per monster—memorise each one before committing to burst combos.",
      "Keep one Wirebug charge or wound pop in reserve; spending all mobility resources simultaneously is the most common wipe cause in 4-player quests.",
      "Part breaks dictate punish economy—targeting a specific wound opens a guaranteed down window worth 3–4 extra hits versus random targeting.",
      "Cycle mantles on a fixed timer (roughly every 90 seconds) rather than waiting for near-death; proactive deployment covers phase transitions smoothly.",
      "In co-op, stagger rotations between hunter roles: binder, DPS, and off-healer positions prevent simultaneous knockback chains."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "怒り移行の予兆（目の光り方・オーラ出現・咆哮モーション）はモンスターごとに異なる。バースト連携前に必ず把握する。",
      "ワイヤーバグや傷付け起爆は1つ以上温存する。全て使い切った状態での全滅が4人クエストで最も多い。",
      "特定部位の傷付けは確定ダウンを呼び込む。狙わないランダム破壊より3〜4ヒット多く入る。",
      "マントルは残量ではなく固定インターバル（約90秒）でローテーションする。フェーズ移行に先手を打てる。",
      "協力プレイでは拘束役・火力役・補助役を明示的に分担し、同時吹き飛びチェーンを防ぐ。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "First Contact: Scout and Bait",
        "body": "Spend the first two minutes scouting the monster's patrol route before placing traps. Wilds monsters have wider roaming ranges than previous entries; committing traps at spawn points wastes setup time. Use the Scoutfly tracking menu to identify the resting position and anchor your first engagement there—rested monsters start with lower stamina thresholds, making the first topple window arrive 15–20% faster."
      },
      {
        "title": "Weapon Sharpening Window",
        "body": "Maintain Blue sharpness minimum for status weapons and White for raw builds. Use the flinch-free phase right after a successful trap detonation or knockdown to sharpen rather than extending damage combos. High-rank field bosses heavily penalise bouncing hits, and losing sharpness tiers during burst windows costs more DPS than the extra combo would have gained."
      },
      {
        "title": "Slinger Burst Setup",
        "body": "Stock Puddle Pods and Brightmoss before entering the quest area. Puddle Pods trigger Mud status in Coral Highlands zones, enabling free repositioning. Brightmoss reveals wound locations on obscured body parts. Prioritise collecting slinger ammo from environmental nodes during the early low-aggro window when the monster is still patrolling."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Wound Management Rotation",
        "body": "Each weapon type opens and pops wounds differently. Greatsword and Hammer create wounds fastest through charged attacks, while Dual Blades benefit most from already-opened wounds. Coordinate wound creation with the party's highest DPS weapon: one player opens, two players punish, one player maintains crowd control. Popping wounds during enrage grants an additional topple, resetting the aggro cycle."
      },
      {
        "title": "Mantle and Item Cycling",
        "body": "Temporal Mantle covers the top 3 multi-hit attacks in each monster's kit—identify those attacks in the first five minutes and time Temporal exclusively for them. Rocksteady handles sustained AoE fields. Never overlap both mantles; if one expires early, maintain a 30-second stagger between activations so coverage gaps don't coincide with enrage phase."
      },
      {
        "title": "Rage Phase Positioning",
        "body": "In enrage, many monsters extend attack chains by 1–2 additional hits and tighten turn speeds. Adjust to 30–40° lateral positioning instead of tail-end positioning to avoid the extended cleave radius. Hammer and Lance players should shift to stagger-interrupt builds that cancel the second wind-up of combo chains rather than attempting full punish sequences."
      },
      {
        "title": "Environment Exploitation",
        "body": "Each map zone in Wilds contains interactive terrain features: falling boulders, mudpools, venom thorns. Memorise two triggerable hazards per zone—these provide free stagger that does not depend on your own positioning. Venom thorns in the Scarlet Forest inflict 4-tick poison even on elder dragon-class monsters immune to Poison status, functioning as flat damage over time instead."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Final 20%: Desperation Attack Set",
        "body": "Sub-20% HP triggers a unique desperation mode with expanded hitbox radius on charged attacks. Reduce your own burst windows from 4-hit to 2-hit safe finishers. The exception: after a topple caused by a wound pop in this phase, the monster's recovery animation is 12 frames longer than earlier phases, giving time for one additional full combo."
      },
      {
        "title": "Capture vs. Kill Calculus",
        "body": "Capture when the capture indicator triggers (limping + green subtarget icon). Capture yields 1–2 extra carve rolls with higher rate for unique parts. Kill is preferable only when targeting head-mount specific drops unavailable in capture pools. Prepare Tranq Bombs and Shock Trap in the Item Bar before the 20% threshold—reactive setup under pressure causes missed windows."
      },
      {
        "title": "Post-Quest Material Routing",
        "body": "For High Rank armour efficiency, prioritise quests that give Apex monster + subspecies drops in the same run. Wilds' layered mission system allows chaining investigations with overlapping target monsters. Tracking node data from completed quests persists into the next session, so ending a session mid-investigation still banks partial scout progress."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Overcommitting after roar or stun recovery—most monsters have a 3-frame \"false recovery\" animation before the real one; attacking on the false frame trades into the next hit.",
      "Using all survival items (Mega Potions, Lifepowder) before the final phase—the desperation attack set deals 40–60% more damage than baseline, so healing capacity must be kept for that window.",
      "Popping wounds with no party member positioned for the topple follow-up—a wasted topple is equivalent to missing a full burst window.",
      "Ignoring elemental zone transitions—monster resistances shift when they move between biomes (e.g., fire-type gains ice weakness in blizzard zones). Not updating loadout element between biome crossings loses 25–30% effective DPS.",
      "Stacking the same debuff (Sleep, Stun) without resetting timers—applying Sleep on a monster that had Sleep applied within the last 90 seconds gives 50% shorter duration."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "咆哮・気絶復帰直後に追撃しすぎる。多くのモンスターは「偽復帰」3フレームの後に本復帰するため、偽復帰で攻撃すると次攻撃と相打ちになる。",
      "終盤前にメガポーション・いのちの粉塵を使い切る。絶望攻撃セットは通常比40〜60%増しのダメージを出す。回復アイテムは最終局面まで温存する。",
